[    7.8s] '? Paste the README now:' -> "\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\tCyberPatriot\n\n\t\t\t\tThe National Youth Cyber Education Program\n\n\t\t\t\t\xa0An Air & Space Forces Association Program\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tVolunteer Sign InRegister Now\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\tPrimary Menu-->\n\nCyberPatriot Competition\nCompetition Overview\nCompetition Schedule\n\nCompetition Fees\n\nGetting Started\nNew Coach Resources\n\nJoin the Competition\n\nCurrent Competition\nRegistered Teams\n\nChallenges and Scoring Values\n\nCompetition Scores\n\nCompetition FAQ\n\nPast Competitions\n\nRules Book\n\nTechnical Specifications\n\nTraining Materials\nStarter Training Modules\n\nWindows Tools\n\nLinux Tools\n\nCisco Training\n\nAdditional Resources\n\nAFA CyberCamps\nCyberCamps Login\n\nAFA CyberCamp Overview\n\nAttend an AFA CyberCamp\n\nHost an AFA CyberCamp\n\n2026 AFA CyberCamp Information\n\nCyber Security Awareness\nCyber Education Literature Series\nSarah the Cyber Hero\n\nBen the Cyber Defender\n\nElementary School Cyber Education Initiative\n\nCyberGenerations\nCyberGenerations Virtual Workshops\n\nTech Caregiver Program\n\nIn The Media\nThe CyberSentinel\n\nPress Releases\n\nRecruitment and Outreach Materials\n\nVideos\n\nAbout Us\nWhat is CyberPatriot?\n\nSponsors\n\nCenters of Excellence\n\nContact Us\n\nBranding Guide & Logos\n\n\t\t\n\n\t\n\n\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\tCyberPatriot Introductory Round & Round 2 Debian 12 README\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\nPlease read the entire README thoroughly before modifying anything on this computer.\n\nUnique Identifier\n\nIf you have not yet entered a valid Unique Identifier, please do so immediately by double clicking on the “CyberPatriot Set Unique Identifier” icon on the desktop. If you do not enter a valid Unique Identifier this VM may stop functioning after a short period of time.\n\nForensics Questions\n\nIf there are “Forensics Questions” on your Desktop, you will receive points for answering these questions correctly. Valid (scored) “Forensics Questions” will only be located directly on your Desktop. Please read all “Forensics Questions” thoroughly before modifying this computer, as you may change something that prevents you from answering the question correctly.\n\nCompetition Scenario\n\nYou work for Arc Foundry & Aerospace (AFA), an aerospace contractor that designs reactor and propulsion systems, fabricates airframes, and runs its own flight-test and certification program. AFA has just acquired a small avionics lab.\n\nAFA’s security policies require that all user accounts be password protected. Employees are required to choose secure passwords, however this policy may not be currently enforced on this computer. The presence of any non-work related media files and “hacking tools” on any computers is strictly prohibited. This company currently does not use any centralized maintenance or polling tools to manage their IT equipment. This computer is for official business use only by authorized users. Your job is to secure this computer, within the guidelines of the scenario, while ensuring the availability of authorized business critical software and services.\n\nDebian 12\n\nIt is company policy to use only Debian 12 on this computer. It is also company policy to use only the latest, official, stable Debian 12 packages available for required software and services on this computer. Management has decided that the default web browser for all users on this computer should be the latest stable version of Chromium. The only company approved firewall for this computer is UFW. The display manager should remain set to LightDM.\n\nCompany policy is to never let users log in as root. If administrators need to run commands as root, they are required to use the “sudo” command.\n\nAll authorized users must be able to log in remotely using SSH. Therefore, sshd is a critical service and needs to remain enabled.\n\nCritical Services:\n\nsshd\n\nBefore you make any changes on the system, please ensure that the passwords below are securely saved and can been accessed when needed to sign in to your account.\n\nAuthorized Administrators and Users\n\nAuthorized Administrators:\npparker (you)\n\tpassword: Fr13ndlyN31ghb0r!\ntstark\n\tpassword: 1AmIr0nM4n!\nppotts\n\tpassword: RunTh3C0mp4ny!\nhhogan\n\tpassword: security1\nnfury\n\tpassword: D1r3ct0r0fSH13LD\nmhill\n\tpassword: D3putyD1r3ct0r!\npcoulson\n\tpassword: V1nt4g3Tr4d1ngC4rds\n\nAuthorized Users:\nbbanner\nswilson\nsstrange\nslang\ncdanvers\nokoye\nkbishop\nybelova\njfoster\nnleeds\nmjwatson\njtorres\npcarter\n\nCompetition Guidelines\n\nIn order to provide a better competition experience, you are NOT required to change the password of the primary, auto-login, user account. Changing the password of a user that is set to automatically log in may lock you out of your computer.\n\nAuthorized administrator passwords were correct the last time you did a password audit, but are not guaranteed to be currently accurate.\n\nDo not stop or disable the CCS Client service or process.\n\nDo not remove any authorized users or their home directories.\n\nThe time zone of this image is set to UTC. Please do not change the time zone, date, or time on this image.\n\nYou can view your current scoring report by double-clicking the “CyberPatriot Scoring Report” desktop icon.\n\nJavaScript is required for some error messages that appear on the “CyberPatriot Scoring Report.” To ensure that you only receive correct error messages, please do not disable JavaScript.\n\nSome security settings may prevent the Stop Scoring application from running. If this happens, the safest way to stop scoring is to suspend the virtual machine. You should NOT power on the VM again before deleting.\n\nThe CyberPatriot Competition System is the property of the Air & Space Forces Association.\n\nCopyright © 2026. All rights reserved.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\n\tREMINDERS\n\n\tTraining Round 2: Oct. 30 - Jan. 19 \n\n\t\n\n\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tCyberPatriot\n1201 Joyce Street, C6\nArlington, VA 22202\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t877-885-5716\ninfo@uscyberpatriot.org\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0©2026 AFA, All Rights Reserved\nCyberPatriot's Privacy Policy\xa0 - \xa0Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information\n\n\t\t\n\n\t" (rule)
